<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/09c30db42c64> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "California prosecutors filed two felony charges against the owner of Tesla Model S for a deadly crash in 2019 that involved the vehicle’s Autopilot system." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "9436" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/dc8283be3c91> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Prosecutors said the Tesla's Autopilot features including autosteer and traffic aware cruise control were being used when the driver crashed into the Honda." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1539" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/0086307ca2f2> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Riad, a limousine service driver, will now face two charges of vehicular manslaughter, according to charges filed with the California Superior Court." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "9436" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/0a5851397c86> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Rafaela Vasquez, the driver in the Uber autonomous test vehicle, was charged in 2020 with negligent homicide after the SUV fatally struck a pedestrian in suburban Phoenix in 2018." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "9435" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/25d91f18c1a6> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "According to the LA County District Attorney, the incident took place in Gardena, a suburb of LA, on December 29, 2019." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "9436" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/265956871f0e> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Donald Slavik, a Colorado lawyer who has served as a consultant in automotive technology lawsuits, including many against Tesla, said he, too, is unaware of any previous felony charges being filed against a U.S. driver who was using partially automated driver technology involved in a fatal crash." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "9435" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/3c870159a17e> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "NHTSA and the National Transportation Safety Board have been reviewing the widespread misuse of Autopilot by drivers, whose overconfidence and inattention have been blamed for multiple crashes, including fatal ones." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1322" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/4e4bb98935be> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "But this admonition doesn't fully come across in the way that Tesla's CEO, Elon Musk, talks about so-called FSD." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "9552" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/579953c12db1> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Los Angeles County prosecutors filed the charges in October, but they came to light only last week." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "9435" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/62fd96a63819> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Bryant Walker Smith, a law professor at the University of South Carolina who studies automated vehicles, said this is the first U.S. case to his knowledge in which serious criminal charges were filed in a fatal crash involving a partially automated driver-assist system." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1322" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/6c962c75e5fb> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Last year, the National Highway Traffic Safety Administration opened an investigation into over a dozen incidents involving Tesla vehicles using Autopilot that have crashed into stationary emergency vehicles." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "9436" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/726f86b1f043> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Los Angeles County prosecutors filed the charges in October, but they came to light only last week." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1322" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/7a710bd69319> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Kevin George Aziz Riad, 27, was exiting a highway in his black Model S when he ran through a red light, slamming into a Honda Civic and killing two people." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "9436" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/87837e6c3320> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "But the National Highway Traffic Safety Administration, which sent investigators to the crash, confirmed last week that Autopilot was in use in the Tesla at the time of the crash." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1322" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/8daaa733673b> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Authorities in Arizona filed a charge of negligent homicide in 2020 against a driver Uber had hired to take part in the testing of a fully autonomous vehicle on public roads." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1322" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/9b504d8e3d81> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Arizona prosecutors declined to file criminal charges against Uber." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1322" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/a22a8bd70371> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Donald Slavik, a Colorado lawyer who has served as a consultant in automotive technology lawsuits, including many against Tesla, said he, too, is unaware of any previous felony charges being filed against a U.S. driver who was using partially automated driver technology involved in a fatal crash." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1322" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/b6159f30d1a1> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "NHTSA and the National Transportation Safety Board have been reviewing the widespread misuse of Autopilot by drivers, whose overconfidence and inattention have been blamed for multiple crashes, including fatal ones." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "9435" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/d814deaa4e5f> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Authorities in Arizona filed a charge of negligent homicide in 2020 against a driver Uber had hired to take part in the testing of a fully autonomous vehicle on public roads." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "9435" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/d87fa4e3f32f> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The misuse of Autopilot, which can control steering, speed and braking, has occurred on numerous occasions and is the subject of investigations by two federal agencies." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "9435" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/e28c8cb61e87> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The driver, Kevin George Aziz Riad, 27, has pleaded not guilty." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "9435" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/f332c981b411> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Rafaela Vasquez, the driver in the Uber autonomous test vehicle, was charged in 2020 with negligent homicide after the SUV fatally struck a pedestrian in suburban Phoenix in 2018." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1322" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/f85194ba6678> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The National Highway Traffic Safety Administration, which sent investigators to the crash, confirmed last week that Autopilot was in use in the Tesla at the time of the crash." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "9435" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/516849299278> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The National Highway Traffic Safety Administration is examining a dozen crashes that involved Tesla drivers using Autopilot features amid scrutiny over its advanced driver-assistance functions." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1539" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/74c08881e1d1> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Autopilot is considered a Level 2 “partially automated” system by the Society of Automotive Engineers’ standards, which requires that drivers keep their hands on the wheel and eyes on the road." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "9436" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/8eef4d1d4c9a> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Since the Autopilot crashes began, Tesla has updated the software to try to make it harder for drivers to abuse it." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "9435" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/23837fba4baf> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Tesla warns that drivers need to keep their eyes on the road and hands on the wheel at all times, though the automaker has declined to include a more robust driver-monitoring system (like infrared eye tracking, for example) to ensure its customers are following safety protocols.",
        "Tesla warns that drivers need to keep their eyes on the road and hands on the wheel at all times, though the automaker has declined to include a more robust driver-monitoring system." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "9436" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/5839176d4392> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "2 people who were in the Civic, Gilberto Alcazar Lopez and Maria Guadalupe Nieves-Lopez died at the scene." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "9435" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/5996d2f9887e> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "State prosecutors believe there's enough evidence to try Kevin George Aziz Riad, 27, on two felony counts of vehicular manslaughter, each carrying a prison sentence of up to six years in California." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "9552" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/a998cf72033c> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "2 people who were in the Civic, Gilberto Alcazar Lopez and Maria Guadalupe Nieves-Lopez died at the scene." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1322" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/c63f02acc064> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Bryant Walker Smith, a law professor at the University of South Carolina who studies automated vehicles, said this is the first U.S. case to his knowledge in which serious criminal charges were filed in a fatal crash involving a partially automated driver-assist system." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "9435" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/cfeb7f3737f0> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Tesla's official reply in such cases is that Autopilot and its \"Full Self-Driving\" systems can't drive themselves, so drivers have to be prepared to retake control of their cars at any time." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "9552" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/e61e488114fb> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "It has prompted Congress and NHTSA to look into autonomous vehicle systems in the U.S., while lawmakers abroad try to agree on regulations, too." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "9552" .

